{"companyInfo": {"Updated": "9/29/26", "Footnote": "Figures are for latest twelve months ended June 30, 2026. Market value as of Aug. 18, 2026", "Country/Territory": "U.S.", "Headquarters": "Phoenix", "Industry": "Mining, Crude-Oil Production", "CEO": "Kathleen L. Quirk", "Website": "https://fcx.com", "Ticker": "FCX", "Company type": "Public", "Revenues ($M)": "$25,868", "Profits ($M)": "$2,945", "Market value ($M)": "$95,237", "Number of employees": "29,000", "StockQuote": "NYSE"}, "description": "Phoenix-based Freeport-McMoRan was founded more than 100 years ago in Freeport, Texas, as a sulfur-mining company. The company merged in 1981 with McMoRan Oil and Gas as a fossil fuel and mining conglomerate under the Freeport-McMoRan name. In more recent years, the company has focused its business on metals mining, specifically with a goal of becoming the world leader in copper, which is growing in demand because of its use in renewable energy, electric vehicles, data centers, and more. With a global mining footprint throughout the Americas\u2014from Arizona to Chile\u2014and in Indonesia, Freeport also mines heavily in gold and molybdenum, which is used in steel and other alloys.", "dataTables": [{"changeHeader": "", "footnote": "", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "valueHeader": "", "values": [{"change": null, "title": "Sector", "value": "Natural resources"}, {"change": null, "title": "Industry", "value": "Mining, Crude-Oil Production"}, {"change": null, "title": "Industry Rank", "value": "1"}, {"change": null, "title": "Previous Industry Rank", "value": "6"}, {"change": null, "title": "Overall Score", "value": "6.77"}, {"change": null, "title": "Innovation", "value": "2"}, {"change": null, "title": "People Management", "value": "2"}, {"change": null, "title": "Use of Corporate Assets", "value": "1"}, {"change": null, "title": "Social Responsibility", "value": "5"}, {"change": null, "title": "Quality of Management", "value": "2"}, {"change": null, "title": "F