nt-weight: 400;\">The Phoenix-based mining company supplies about 9% of the world\u2019s mined copper and is led by CEO and board chair Richard Adkerson. FCX has </span><a href=\"https://www.fcx.com/about/board-of-directors\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">12 members</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on its board, including David Abney, former CEO of UPS; Lydia Kennard, CEO of KDG Construction Consulting; and John Stephens, former AT&amp;T CFO. In February, the company appointed its president, Kathleen Quirk, to the board. FCX has grappled with an ongoing </span><a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/markets/commodities/copper-miner-freeport-mcmoran-beats-profit-estimates-2023-04-21/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">labor shortage</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in the copper mining industry in recent months. Its metals are critical to support decarbonization efforts and the green energy transition. In its 2022</span><a href=\"https://www.fcx.com/sustainability\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> sustainability report</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u2014its 22nd to date\u2014the company outlined its ESG performance, covering human rights, responsible supply-chain practices, and ethics, among other matters. There are five women members on its 12-person board.</span>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 171, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "100-fastest-growing-companies", "title": "100 Fastest-Growing Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 68, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 157, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank"